                      "text": "All-purpose wheat flour has a bulk density of ~0.528 g/mL (7.81 grams per US tablespoon). 15 grams of AP flour is approximately 1.92 US tablespoons (nearly 2 level tablespoons or 5.75 teaspoons)."
                    }
